diff --git a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
index a4f48b5..07c08e2 100644
--- a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
+++ b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
@@ -159,3 +159,46 @@ __Response:__
 ```
 
 `request` and `response` can be `null` for deliveries that have not started yet or are still in progress. The delivery request headers omit the `X-Webhook-Signature` header.
+
+## Deliveries
+
+When an event happens on a board, Fizzy POSTs a JSON representation of it to every
+active webhook on that board that subscribed to the event's action. Each event is
+delivered exactly once: there are no retries, so a receiver that is down misses the
+events that happened while it was unreachable.
+
+__Request:__
+
+```
+POST https://api.example.com/webhooks
+User-Agent: fizzy/1.0.0 Webhook
+Content-Type: application/json
+X-Webhook-Timestamp: 2025-12-05T19:36:35.401Z
+X-Webhook-Signature: 1a2b3c...
+
+{"id":"03f5v9zkft4hj9qq0lsn9ohde","action":"card_published","created_at":"...","eventable":{...},"board":{...},"creator":{...}}
+```
+
+The body is the same event representation the API uses for
+[`GET /:account_slug/events`](sections/events.md).
+
+`X-Webhook-Signature` is the `HMAC` `SHA256` digest of the request body, keyed with the
+webhook's `signing_secret`. Verify it before trusting a delivery.
+
+## The delivery log
+
+Every attempt is logged as a delivery, whether it went well or not. A delivery is
+`pending` until it's handed to the queue, `in_progress` while the request is being made,
+and then either `completed` (we got a response) or `errored` (we never got one).
+
+A delivery is successful when it completed with a `2XX` response. Anything else — a `4XX`
+or `5XX` response, or an error — counts as a failure.
+
+The log is kept for a week.
+
+## Switching a webhook off
+
+A receiver that keeps failing is switched off after ten failures in a row that have been
+going on for over an hour. Its deliveries keep being logged, but nothing is sent anymore
+until an account admin reactivates it. Reactivating a webhook starts counting failures
+from scratch.
